& [RestoredRegistry]
  + construct one new cantor-succeeding-sop-fixture-registry-record/0.1 selecting the rollback revision and source from the B2A predecessor snapshot
  + restored snapshot uses the commissioned distinct snapshot identity exact registry identity current physical generation plus one predecessor revision digest predecessor source path supplied evidence and a recomputed snapshot digest
  + restored registry binds exact fixture root activation authority recovery owner B2A transaction and restored snapshot with a separate registry-record digest
  + generation advances monotonically; rollback never rewinds the registry generation or reuses the predecessor snapshot identity

& [Persistence]
  + deterministic restored-registry machine bytes end in one LF and create_new the exact absent same-parent temporary path
  + ordered execution is write_all file sync_all temporary reopen exact compare safe same-volume rename replacement parent directory sync_all and final reopen parse digest and exact compare
  + before replacement remove only a temporary file created by the current attempt on failure
  + after replacement any validation or durability failure reports replacement_performed true and never claims atomic refusal automatic rollback boot success or cleanup
  + Windows directory-flush Access Denied remains a typed post-replacement durability refusal; no unsafe handle wrapper or weakened durability is authorized

& [Receipt]
